From 91162c6457181755dea6ab15603a33e4e191d8aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:47:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fork: build schedule cadence from intervals, times, days and
 cron

Replace the five cadence presets in the schedule sheet with a cadence
builder: Interval (optionally inside set hours and days), Daily at
several times, Weekly days, Monthly on a day or the nth weekday, and a
custom Cron field. Every mode compiles to one five-field cron the
daemon already runs, so no wire change is needed.

- A saved expression opens in a builder mode only when compiling that
  mode gives back the exact expression; anything else opens as Cron.
  Untouched cadences and limits are never resent on edit.
- Cron cadences without a time zone open in UTC, where the daemon runs
  them. Legacy rolling intervals stay untouched until changed.
- The time zone is pickable. The preview lists upcoming runs and a
  14-day strip computed with the daemon's own matcher, now shared from
  protocol (findNextCronMatch), including fall-back repeats,
  spring-forward skips and short months.
- Ends: never, after a date (expiresAt at local midnight after the
  date) or after N runs (maxRuns, counted against finished runs loaded
  with schedule/inspect on edit).
- Host offline and save failures show an alert; cadences that never
  run are blocked.

PASEO-21

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
